## Detailed Rules

### Base image
| Criteria | Rule |
|----------|------|
| Default runtime | `mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0-alpine` |
| Needs ICU (globalization) | `mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0-bookworm-slim` with `DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=false` |
| SDK (build only) | `mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:10.0-alpine` |
| NEVER in production | `sdk:*` in the final image |

> Always pin with **explicit** minor version (`10.0`, not `latest`). In production pipelines, use SHA256 digest.

### Required Environment Variables
```dockerfile
ENV ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:8080
ENV ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production
ENV DOTNET_RUNNING_IN_CONTAINER=true
ENV DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=false   # if using dates/locale
ENV DOTNET_GC_HEAP_HARD_LIMIT_PERCENT=75          # prevents OOM in memory-limited containers
```

### Port
- Expose **only port 8080** (HTTP). TLS is terminated at the ingress/load balancer.
- `EXPOSE 443` only if there is direct mTLS between services.

### Image size
- Target: final image < **200 MB** (Alpine).
- Verify with `docker image inspect <image> --format='{{.Size}}'` and report in CI.
- Remove unnecessary diagnostic tools from runtime.

### Security
- Run as non-root (`USER app`) — required.
- Do not install `curl`, `wget`, or other utilities in the final image (for `HEALTHCHECK`, use `wget` already present in Alpine).
- Scan with `trivy image` in CI — fail if `HIGH` or `CRITICAL` CVE without justified exception.
- Never use `--privileged` or `cap_add` without security approval.

### Build Arguments (ARGs)
```dockerfile
ARG BUILD_CONFIGURATION=Release   # Release | Debug
ARG VERSION=1.0.0                 # Injected by CI (e.g. git tag)
ARG VCS_REF=unknown               # Short git SHA
ARG BUILD_DATE=unknown            # ISO 8601
```
Never use `ARG` for secrets — use `--mount=type=secret` (BuildKit).

### Build-Time Secrets (BuildKit)
If credentials are needed for `dotnet restore` (private NuGet feed):
```dockerfile
RUN --mount=type=secret,id=nuget_token \
    dotnet restore "src/Api/Api.csproj" \
      --configfile NuGet.Config \
      /p:NuGetToken=$(cat /run/secrets/nuget_token) \
      --locked-mode
```

### BuildKit Cache (`--mount=type=cache`)
```dockerfile
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.nuget/packages \
    dotnet restore "src/Api/Api.csproj" --locked-mode
```
Reduces build time by ~40% on repeated local builds.

### HEALTHCHECK
```dockerfile
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=15s --retries=3 \
  CMD wget -qO- http://localhost:8080/health/live || exit 1
```
- `/health/live` → liveness (process alive)
- `/health/ready` → readiness (dependencies ready) — checked by orchestrator, not by native HEALTHCHECK

